WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.020
A creek is full of tiny animals hiding under the rocks.

2
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.220
They eat bits of leaves, and fish eat them, so they all need each other.

3
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.040
Some only live in clean water, so they are clues to how healthy the creek is.

4
00:00:15.983 --> 00:00:21.323
You need a kitchen strainer or small net, a white tray, a plastic spoon, and closed

5
00:00:21.323 --> 00:00:22.923
toe water shoes for everyone.

6
00:00:23.967 --> 00:00:28.727
Pick a creek with a shallow riffle, low and clear, at least three days after heavy

7
00:00:28.727 --> 00:00:33.407
rain. Fill the tray with creek water, about two to three centimeters deep.

8
00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:39.047
Hold the strainer just downstream of a rock while someone lifts the rock and rubs

9
00:00:39.047 --> 00:00:41.827
its underside. Tip the strainer into the tray.

10
00:00:42.727 --> 00:00:44.567
After a minute, specks will start to move.

11
00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:49.007
Finding many different kinds is usually a sign of a healthy creek.

12
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.580
Stay within arm's reach of your child the whole time they are in or beside the

13
00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:59.400
water. Wade only where the water is ankle deep, and slow, never rushing.
